 ## Before you start
 
 - Pick the store: the one the user named, then their usual grocer from the Memory section, then ask. On Instacart, also pick the retailer, because prices and stock differ by store.
-- Read the Memory section for the usual list at that store, brands and sizes they buy, dietary rules and allergies, brands to avoid, organic or other preferences, substitution rules, and household size. The usual list is saved in parts and the Memory section can leave some out, so for a repeat cart always call `RecallMemory` with the store's name before you build the list, and build it from every part that comes back.
+- Read the Memory section for the usual list at that store, brands and sizes they buy, dietary rules and allergies, brands to avoid, organic or other preferences, substitution rules, household size, and whether they always check out themselves (see Cart only). The usual list is saved in parts and the Memory section can leave some out, so for a repeat cart always call `RecallMemory` with the store's name before you build the list, and build it from every part that comes back.
 - Run SearchPlugins for the grocer. Use a connector when one is installed. Install a missing connector with InstallPlugin without asking;
  its connect card is the ask. Ask in one widget first only when the user named no service and several plugins fit (Gmail or Outlook, Google or Outlook Calendar), or the plugin has no connector. Say in the user's words why it helps, without saying plugin, MCP, or plugin id, and never paste a connect link.
 - Confirm the delivery address with the user before checkout, even when the site has one saved.
